# Legwork configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `config` (same directory) and edit. `config` is gitignored.
# suite/legwork_runner.py loads it at startup, so launchd (which does not
# read your shell profile), cron and manual runs share one source of truth.
# Real environment variables always override the file. Values may use $HOME
# and ~, which are expanded. Lines are KEY=VALUE; # starts a comment.
#
# You can also point the runner at a config elsewhere with LEGWORK_CONFIG=/path.

# The install level ./install.sh recorded: 1 is the manual loop (no runner,
# timer or hooks), 2 is autonomy. Only read back by the installer to pre-fill
# the choice on a re-run; the runner ignores it.
# LEGWORK_LEVEL=2

# Where the legwork repo lives. Default: $HOME/legwork.
LEGWORK_DIR=$HOME/legwork

# Autonomous fires per project per calendar day. Default: 8. Counted from
# runner.log, so truncating or rotating that file resets the day's count.
LEGWORK_DAILY_CAP=8

# Optional spend guard, in dollars. Unset or 0 means no cost cap. When set,
# the runner sums today's per-fire costs from runner.log and stops firing for
# the rest of the day once the cap is reached (alerting once, like a stall).
# LEGWORK_DAILY_COST_CAP=10

# --- Review pipeline (OPTIONAL) ---------------------------------------------
# The n8n webhooks the SessionEnd hook and the runner post to. Leave BOTH unset
# to run the queue with no reviewer: the runner still fires sessions and they
# still wrap, the review post and the Telegram alerts are just skipped.
#   LEGWORK_WEBHOOK_URL  receives session evidence for review.
#   LEGWORK_ALERT_URL    receives runner stall alerts and the daily heartbeat.
# LEGWORK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-n8n-host/webhook/legwork-review
# LEGWORK_ALERT_URL=https://your-n8n-host/webhook/legwork-alert

# Local reviewer: the no-n8n alternative to LEGWORK_WEBHOOK_URL. When set (and
# no webhook is configured), the runner triages each finished session in-process
# with a `claude -p` call and writes the pass/revise/escalate verdict straight
# back to the project file, so reviewer-by-exception runs without n8n. The
# webhook wins if both are set. See suite/legwork_review.py.
# LEGWORK_LOCAL_REVIEW=1

# The model the reviewer call uses, for BOTH the local reviewer (read by the
# runner) and the n8n pipeline (read by suite/reviewer/n8n-build-node.js). A full id
# or a short alias. Default: claude-sonnet-4-6.
# REVIEWER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# --- Claude config dirs (OPTIONAL) ------------------------------------------
# Run autonomous sessions under a dedicated Claude config dir, so they never
# inherit whatever account your interactive shell defaults to. Leave unset to
# use the default config. A project may set `account: <name>` in its
# frontmatter; set CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR_<NAME> (uppercased) to give that account
# its own config dir.
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=$HOME/.claude-legwork
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR_WORK=$HOME/.claude-legwork-work

# --- Applied outside the runner (documented here so config lives in one place)
# The launchd tick interval lives in suite/com.legwork.runner.plist
# (StartInterval, seconds). Default: 300 (every 5 minutes).

# --- Orchestration (OPTIONAL) ------------------------------------------------
# Read by the orchestration layer (orchestration/): /fanout, /ship, /bugbot,
# the switchboard-protocol skill and the Hermes switchboard skill. /onboard
# writes them through orchestration/install.py; nothing else needs them.
# See orchestration/README.md.
#
# Set by the installer when fanout or the switchboard is installed.
# LEGWORK_ORCHESTRATION=1
#
# Who relays an orchestrator's DECISIONs: hermes (a Hermes thread, with the
# switchboard skill) or manual (you read .legwork/switchboard.md and type
# answers into the pane yourself). Default: hermes.
# LEGWORK_SWITCHBOARD=hermes
#
# The Hermes profile the switchboard skill was installed into. `default` is
# ~/.hermes itself.
# LEGWORK_HERMES_PROFILE=default
#
# GitHub users or orgs whose repos are yours, comma-separated. On these,
# issue ids may appear in PRs, planning docs go up as PRs and merges may be
# allowed. Every other owner is treated as a shared repo.
# LEGWORK_OWN_OWNERS=your-user,your-org
#
# GitHub owners with Cursor Bugbot installed. /bugbot and /fanout skip the
# Bugbot loop everywhere else, rather than waiting 20 minutes for nothing.
# Unset means no owner has Bugbot.
# LEGWORK_BUGBOT_OWNERS=your-org
#
# Linear: the team every issue lives in, and its key (the PLT in PLT-12).
# Leave unset to skip the Linear rules entirely. Optional sweep labels are
# checked at planning time, e.g. labels another tool files commitments under.
# LEGWORK_LINEAR_TEAM=Platform
# LEGWORK_LINEAR_TEAM_KEY=PLT
# LEGWORK_LINEAR_SWEEP_LABELS=src:slack,src:notion
#
# Your own skills for two jobs, by name, if you have them: writing PR bodies
# (/ship and /fanout's workers use it instead of the built-in shape) and
# verifying a UI journey in a browser (the quality gate uses it instead of
# plain Playwright).
# LEGWORK_PR_SKILL=pr-writer
# LEGWORK_UI_SKILL=ui-check
#
# The usage cache the usage guard and switchboard-wait read. Default: the
# ccstatusline cache at ~/.cache/ccstatusline/usage.json. With no cache the
# usage checks are skipped.
# LEGWORK_USAGE_CACHE=$HOME/.cache/ccstatusline/usage.json
